 # Sample Matching
-
-
 ## Overview
-Sample Matching is a differentiable volume rendering estimator that implements sample matching to reduce variance in gradient estimation for volumetric path tracing [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the high-variance gradient problem in differentiable volume rendering by estimating the transmittance and scattering terms of the Differentiable Radiative Transfer Equation (DRTE) at the same spatial points on each path segment, causing their opposite-sign contributions to cancel [S2, unofficial]. Unlike the base `prbvolpath` method which estimates these terms at unrelated points, Sample Matching confines all modifications to the adjoint pass while keeping the primal image rendering identical [S2, unofficial].
+Sample Matching is a differentiable volume rendering estimator that implements sample matching to reduce variance in gradient estimation for volumetric path tracing [S1, unofficial]. It solves the high-variance gradient problem in differentiable volume rendering by estimating the transmittance and scattering terms of the Differentiable Radiative Transfer Equation (DRTE) at the same spatial points on each path segment, causing their opposite-sign contributions to cancel [S2, unofficial]. Unlike the base `prbvolpath` method which estimates these terms at unrelated points, Sample Matching confines all modifications to the adjoint pass while keeping the primal image rendering identical [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** Primal path trace data (segments, transmittance, scattering contributions) generated by the base `prbvolpath` integrator.
-*   **Output:** Gradient estimates for the extinction grid parameters.
